A||||7||Gokart||Please help! Running terrible!
Z||000000||Gokart||07-17-99||06:32 PM||||It's like someone stole my V6 and put in a lawnmower engine! No engine light but used scanner anyway and got a 44, but just changed O2 sensor! Thought it could be exhaust or cat can so I just spent 400.00 and had both replaced but still runs terrible?!? I'm running out of options until I'll have to break down and bring it to the dealer. Any suggestions? TIA!
Z||000001||Gokart||07-17-99||07:45 PM||||Just needed to add that within the last 2 months I recently changed plugs, wires, cap, rotor, fuel filter and changed oil and was running perfect.
Z||000002||sluppy123||07-17-99||09:21 PM||||Use an ohm meter and check your plug wires for excesive resistance.<p>I'd bought a new set and about a week later the engine started running like crap. I couldn't figure out what was wrong and was ready to take it in to the shop when a friend told me to check the plug wires. 
Z||000003||Gokart||07-18-99||04:09 AM||||Sluppy 123, I don't have an ohm meter, but would it be worth it to change the wires again before I bring it to the dealer?
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||07-18-99||06:46 AM||||GoKart, What do you mean by "running terrible"?<p>An easy (although not very accurate) way to check your plug wires is to disconnect one at the time (when the engine is not running!), start it up and see if it makes any difference. If, after disconnecting a wire, the engine runs the same as before disconnecting it, you have a broken wire.<p>Also disconnect the tachfilter and see if that makes any difference.
Z||000005||Gokart||07-18-99||08:22 AM||||I do have an ohm meter, I didn't know it's also called a digital multi-tester so I'll check the wires. By "running terrible" I mean it's got absolutely no power! Louder than it was before also, thats why I thought it was an exhaust problem. I beginning to suspect that its a fuel injection problem?
Z||000006||batboy||07-18-99||08:39 AM||||After checking all the obvious stuff (like are the plug wires going to the right places, timing is ok, etc...), you may want to do a compression check. I'd check the EGR valve too, just to be on the safe side.
Z||000007||Gokart||07-18-99||08:02 PM||||Welp! Sunday evening is almost over and so is my "tinkering time"! Thanks for suggestions guys. Off to the dealer Monday or Teusday. Can you believe the name of our local Pontiac dealer----BATTLES Pontiac!!  Will let you all know how much the battle will be!
